TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"authorizedComments":[{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \"no commit needed\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z","id":2,"updatedAt":"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z","url":"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2"},{"author":"uid:1000","body":"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE 2 — CHECKPOINT PURITY (all cp-* tasks). The driver fails a checkpoint whose command mutates tracked files on re-run: \"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\" (cp-weights burned 3 attempts on this at 07:03-07:10). Discipline: (1) produce your receipt inside your LANE COMMIT (results/receipts/<name>.json, deterministic content); (2) the checkpoint/acceptance command must be IDEMPOTENT and side-effect-free on tracked paths — on re-run over an already-correct base it re-measures and COMPARES; if facts match the committed receipt it must leave every tracked file byte-identical (reuse the receipt's existing ts — NEVER stamp a fresh timestamp onto an unchanged measurement) and exit 0; (3) scratch output goes to untracked temp paths only; (4) if a repo script must change to achieve this, that edit belongs in your lane commit within your ownership paths. Fail receipts still land under results/receipts/failed/ per doctrine.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z","id":3,"updatedAt":"2026-08-30T05:16:27.726Z","url":"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/3"}],"receipt":{"lateRecheckCommentIds":[],"preparedCommentIds":[2,3],"recheckTruncated":false,"rechecked":true,"source":{"kind":"local-jsonl","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl","preparedCursor":6,"recheckedCursor":6,"registrationId":"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff"}},"taskId":"proxy-tooling"}
